        "mission_intent": "We need to update our maintenance management process for the SecureOps platform to align with NIST SP 800-160 Volume 1 guidance on security aspects of maintenance. Specifically, I'd like the engineering team to design and implement a procedure where all incident and problem reports\u2014including those that are not explicitly security-related\u2014are systematically reviewed to identify any security relevance and to determine associated maintenance needs arising from that review. The procedure should account for the fact that seemingly non-security incidents may still have security implications that aren't immediately obvious, so the triage logic needs to cast a wide net. The identified maintenance needs should be categorized appropriately across corrective, adaptive, perfective, and preventive maintenance types. Additionally, the procedure must feed its findings into the maintenance action workflow so that security considerations are incorporated before any maintenance work is executed. Please draft the process specification, including workflow diagrams and role assignments, and have it ready for review by the systems security engineering lead by end of next sprint. We'll be integrating this into our existing ServiceNow instance for tracking.",
